tests:
  e2e:
    count: 28
    where: "ui/e2e/specs/flows.spec.ts (22) + ui/e2e/specs/onboarding.spec.ts (6), run by cargo xtask ui e2e"
    note: "The epic's own e2e evidence, run here at its close. WebdriverIO drives the real Tauri/WebKit window against an ephemeral run(Config) core. UC-4: a proxied request lands as a row carrying every column, the status carries its reason phrase, the method filter offers verbs rather than free text, a filter narrows and clears, an unmatched filter states the query excludes the traffic, the host filter offers hosts capture has seen, the header row does not wrap, and the keyboard alone selects a row and opens its detail. UC-5: the panel opens on the request leg with headers/timing/versions, the leg selector switches headers and body together, JSON renders copy-exact, raw shows the served source, curl copies and the button reverts, Esc dismisses, a brotli body decodes through the UI, a compressed body's raw is source not hex frames, an image dispatches, an XML body renders as XML, the body stays on screen under a wall of headers with no window scroll, a long header value clamps to three lines with more/less, and an over-cap body states its truncation. UC-ONBOARD: a fresh launch shows onboarding not the list, each step carries a verdict with no prev/next pair, a step opens from its own header one body at a time, a decrypted HTTPS flow flips the last step and reveals the list, the filter narrows and clears, and a second request appends without a refresh. This WU also names the contract onboarding.spec.ts proves - its describe and header said UC-5 while the file proves UC-ONBOARD."
  integration:
    count: 27
    where: "ui/src/App.test.tsx"
    note: "The app mounts against a mock API and resolves its single entry point - the contract the deleted ?gallery guard sat in front of. No new integration file: this WU's bounded contract is that the app still mounts, with one path and no query-string branch, and App.test.tsx is where that is asserted. Its 27 tests are unchanged by the diff and all green."
  unit:
    count: 741
    where: "ui/src/**/*.test.ts(x) - 44 files, cd ui && pnpm test"
    note: "742 in 45 files before, 741 in 44 after. The whole delta is Gallery.test.tsx's single test, deleted with the screen it rendered; every other test is untouched and green. A deletion's unit evidence is the surviving suite - there is no new behaviour to assert, and no test can be written for a file that no longer exists. main.tsx is a bootstrap with no exported behaviour: it is proven by the e2e launching the real window (every spec above starts by mounting the app it renders) and by App.test.tsx mounting what it mounts."
verified:
  - "cargo xtask ui e2e - 28 passing, 2 spec files, 0 failing, in 00:00:07 against a real ephemeral core."
  - "cd ui && pnpm test - 741 passed, 44 files, 0 failed."
  - "cd ui && pnpm exec eslint src - clean, including the design/vocabulary rule over all of ui/src/."
  - "cargo test - green (no core code in this diff). cargo fmt --check and cargo clippy -D warnings green at every commit via the pre-commit hook."
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc over the whole tree - 65 docs checked, none red (re-run at the final tip, after the result report itself landed; the earlier 64 was the tree before it existed), after the rulebook blob moved aeff5b0 -> 849cc8e. The four design runs pin the old blob and stay green because all four are data-status=archived: check_pin exempts an archived run by design (doc.rs:631-635), a run that closed under an older rulebook being a record rather than a stale claim. Verified by running verify-doc after the amendment, not assumed."
  - "cargo xtask design-scope epic/redesign HEAD - one rendered file touched (ui/src/main.tsx), no design artifact in the diff. The deleted Gallery.tsx is not reported as a touched surface, so this WU's cr/v3 carries one design.undesigned entry, not the two its plan predicted."
  - "node scripts/design-registry.mjs - 28 entries, including all three the epic added (Field, StatusDot, Disclosure). No roster entry lost with Gallery.tsx: the screen was a consumer of the registry, never a member of it."
note: "Four review rounds, and every round's fixes carried the next round's defects - which is the argument for running another. Round 3: three candidates, two refuted on evidence (the E-DFLOW.W11 coverage-map attribution, traced through that epic's own result report where 30 inherited + 1 retired + 1 answered gives the 32 assertions the plan cites; and DEC-34's note on Tier-1 blindness, which names wrap-not-truncate where DEC-26 measured check_vocabulary - a distinct predicate and a lineage, not a duplicate), one fixed: the review table itself had three findings packed into one cell, against the rule that a wall of text fails review. Round 4, a confirming pass over the whole diff, found the arithmetic of round 3's own row - it read 0 verified while recording the fix it had just made - and re-checked the rulebook blob, the href sweep, the doc count, design-scope, the registry roster and the unit suite clean against the tree. Round 2 found three, all in round 1's own fixes and its documents rather than in code - the reason the round exists. The one that mattered: docs/use-cases/web-ui.html linked the flow-list design run by <a href>, a permanent T2 record pointing into a file DEC-3 deletes at the epic close, so the archive move would have 404'd it and reddened verify-doc's link check at the epic gate; an earlier version of this WU's doc/v1 note asserted no such link existed, without running the sweep that would have found it. Now rewritten as plain text marked archived, and the sweep (grep for href into work/ across every T1/T2 doc) returns nothing. The other two: the result's Evidence row still read 64 docs where its own review section already said 65, and the refuted-claims table restated the follow-up row beside it. Round 1 of the review found one verified defect, in this WU's own new decision record rather than in its code: DEC-34 rejected a hypothetical violated-by-constraint verdict as `a seventh verdict` when the receipt enum already holds seven (VERDICTS in xtask/src/doc.rs) and DEC-15 names it a fixed seven-verdict enum - so an addition is the eighth. Fixed, and the rejection now cites DEC-15. Two further candidates were refuted on evidence: the note's earlier `64 docs checked` described the tree before this WU's own result report existed (a doc cannot verify a tree containing its own unwritten bytes; the count above is the re-run over all 65 and is green), and the epic plan's two deferred items belong to the epic result report's follow-ups by the work-planning standard's own split, not to a WU report - they are carried in the result so the trail cannot break. Simplification and efficiency returned nothing; the efficiency finder built production bundles at both endpoints and found the guarded Gallery branch was already eliminated by Vite's DEV static-replace before this WU, so the deletion is a source-tree cleanup and no bundle claim is made anywhere. The plan's unit prediction was wrong and is corrected here rather than in prose only: it said 44 files / 731 tests after the deletion, on an unchecked assumption about how many tests Gallery.test.tsx held. It held one. The suite is 741. Nothing else in the plan's test table moved."
